Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 02:03:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/44] feat: ISO film grain, exposure response, servo zoom for
 CinematicCamera

- ISO-driven film grain via FilterGrain_Amount: early-onset + cubic
  top-end noise curve, baseline shifted by sensor size (SNR scales with
  linear sensor dimension: full frame +0, APS-C +0.6, M43 +1.1 stops),
  boosted when the lens is starved of light (t/N^2 vs f/5.6 at 1/50).
- Exposure Response + Neutral EV: compress applied EV around a pivot so
  aperture/EV feel like a processed camera image; 1.0 = strict physics.
- Servo zoom motor: quantised focal targets are approached in log space
  over Focal Step Time instead of snapping (real zoom optics cannot jump
  focal length); FOV, DOF and blur all follow the eased value.
- ICinematicCameraOptics gains SetISO/GetISO.
- Opt-in ActivateOnGameStart (see earlier fix) retained.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
